The luna theme's faces (~/.config/themes/luna/).

Tahoma -- the UI face (theme.conf font=): the bar, the toolbox, the popup
    panels, the launcher, mako, mpv's OSD and subtitles, the LLM chat's
    headings, Nautilus's document face.
    This is WINE's Tahoma, not Microsoft's file. Wine ships its own
    replacement so Windows programs that ask for "Tahoma" by name get a
    face with the right metrics: drawn by Larry Snyder in 2004 from
    Bitstream Vera Sans, renamed as Vera's licence requires, and kept in
    Wine's source tree as FontForge .sfd files. Its family name is exactly
    "Tahoma" (PostScript names WineTahoma / WineTahomaBold), which is why
    the stylesheets can just say Tahoma. Nothing here comes from Windows.
    Regular and Bold, both with tabular figures (every digit 1118/2048 em in
    Regular, 1304/2048 in Bold, read with fontTools), so the bar's clock and
    readouts never twitch and need no min-width. Tahoma's metrics, not
    Vera's: narrower than IBM Plex Sans, with a 1.21 em line against Plex's
    1.30, so most panels come out a little shorter than cyberpunk's --
    ~/.config/themes/luna/panel.css's header has the measured sizes.
    Coverage: Latin and Cyrillic (846 code points in Regular); no Greek and
    no arrows. IBM Plex Sans is the per-glyph fallback (theme.conf font=
    lists it second), Font Awesome the icon fallback as everywhere.
    Files:  tahoma.ttf, tahomabd.ttf   (built here, see below)
            tahoma.sfd, tahomabd.sfd   (the sources, kept for a rebuild)
    Source: https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/raw/wine-9.0/fonts/tahoma.sfd
            https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/raw/wine-9.0/fonts/tahomabd.sfd
            (Wine tag wine-9.0)
    Licence: LGPL-2.1-or-later, as part of Wine:
                COPYING.LIB          https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/raw/wine-9.0/COPYING.LIB
                LICENSE-wine.txt     https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/raw/wine-9.0/LICENSE
             plus the Bitstream Vera licence for the base design:
                LICENSE-Bitstream-Vera.txt   the Vera section of
                https://raw.githubusercontent.com/dejavu-fonts/dejavu-fonts/master/LICENSE
                (DejaVu quotes it verbatim; only that section is kept)

    Built with the installed FontForge (20251009), one call per weight:
        fontforge -lang=ff -c 'Open($1); Generate($2)' tahoma.sfd tahoma.ttf
        fontforge -lang=ff -c 'Open($1); Generate($2)' tahomabd.sfd tahomabd.ttf
    (FontForge warns about unused Arabic glyphs in a lookup subtable; the
    face has no Arabic, so the warning is harmless.)

    Then ONE metrics fix, the only change to Wine's design: the .sfd sets
    USE_TYPO_METRICS with typo metrics that add up to exactly 1.0 em
    (ascender 1566, descender -423, gap 59 of 2048), so Pango -- which
    honours that flag -- set every line solid: panels came out 12-16%
    shorter than cyberpunk's, accents touching the line above. Windows lays
    Tahoma out by its win metrics (2049 / 423, a 1.21 em line), so the typo
    and hhea metrics are set to those and the flag cleared, with fontTools
    (python3-fonttools). The same step writes a change notice INTO each
    font (name ID 10, the description), as LGPL-2.1 section 2(b) asks of a
    modified file, so the notice travels with the .ttf even without this
    README; the family "Tahoma" and the PostScript names are kept, so the
    stylesheets and fontconfig still match. For each of tahoma.ttf and
    tahomabd.ttf (STEM = tahoma / tahomabd):
        python3 -I - IN.ttf OUT.ttf STEM <<'PY'
        import sys
        from fontTools.ttLib import TTFont
        f = TTFont(sys.argv[1]); o, h = f["OS/2"], f["hhea"]
        o.sTypoAscender, o.sTypoDescender, o.sTypoLineGap = o.usWinAscent, -o.usWinDescent, 0
        o.fsSelection &= ~(1 << 7)
        h.ascent, h.descent, h.lineGap = o.usWinAscent, -o.usWinDescent, 0
        note = (f"Modified 2026-10-24 from Wine's {sys.argv[3]}.sfd (wine-9.0) for the Atrium "
                "luna theme: OS/2 typo and hhea metrics set to the win metrics, "
                "USE_TYPO_METRICS cleared. No outline changed.")
        f["name"].setName(note, 10, 3, 1, 0x409)
        f["name"].setName(note, 10, 1, 0, 0)
        f.save(sys.argv[2])
        PY
    Then
        fc-cache -f ~/.local/share/fonts
    and checked with `fc-list | grep -i tahoma`: family Tahoma, styles
    Regular and Bold.

Liberation Mono -- the terminal face (term.font=, font_mono=): COSMIC
    Terminal, kitty, mpv's console, code in the LLM chat, Nautilus's
    monospace. Courier New's metrics, the XP console's TrueType choice;
    Regular / Bold / Italic / Bold Italic, spacing=100.
    NOT copied here: it is a Fedora package. At fetch time
    `rpm -q liberation-mono-fonts` = liberation-mono-fonts-2.1.5-15.fc44.noarch
    (licence OFL-1.1-RFN). If it is ever removed:
    `sudo dnf install liberation-mono-fonts`, or upstream at
    https://github.com/liberationfonts/liberation-fonts (OFL).

